[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4708507874","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4708507874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4708507874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGKYg4g","user":{"login":"web-max","id":66029945,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MDI5OTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66029945?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max","html_url":"https://github.com/web-max","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T13:38:54Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T13:38:54Z","body":"This is a really good question","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4708507874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4709273726","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4709273726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4709273726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGLHQfg","user":{"login":"DietrichGebert","id":137048761,"node_id":"U_kgDOCCsyuQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137048761?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T15:00:41Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T15:00:41Z","body":"Fair ask, honest answer: I haven't run SWE-Bench Pro or Terminal Bench. The current benchmark measures code size, cost, latency, and a correctness gate on five everyday tasks, not task-success on a full agentic harness.\n\nMy prior for SWE-Bench: ponytail shouldn't move resolution rate much, because it explicitly refuses to simplify away correctness, validation, security, or anything requested. It trims over-engineering, not the fix. The delta I'd expect is in tokens/cost per solved instance. But that's a hypothesis, not a number, and I won't put an unmeasured number in the README. If anyone wants to wire ponytail in as a SWE-Bench arm, I'm very interested either way.\n\nRelated: v4.6.0 just shipped a local-model run showing the LOC win evaporates on a 3B model, so the effect is clearly model-dependent.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4709273726/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4709918388","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4709918388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4709918388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGLumtA","user":{"login":"guplem","id":11029629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDI5NjI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11029629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem","html_url":"https://github.com/guplem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T16:11:38Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T16:11:38Z","body":"I've seen many system prompts that reduce token usage, explain things clearly, and plan better. But I never see them tested against benchmarks, so how can we know they’re working?\n\nI’ve so far refused to use any because I always think, \"_If they were as good, they would be added to ClaudeCode, OpenCode, Codex, and so on_.\" \n\nSo maybe they aren’t as good, but how much worse are they? If they’re 95% there and reduce usage by more than 80%, I would instantly switch!\n\nBut since there are no official benchmarks run, here I am, taking a look at the prompts to see if I can improve my system prompts a bit ^^'","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4709918388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4710311819","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4710311819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4710311819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGMGniw","user":{"login":"Tobbe","id":30793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe","html_url":"https://github.com/Tobbe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tobbe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T17:00:58Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T17:01:39Z","body":"> I’ve so far refused to use any because I always think, \"_If they were as good, they would be added to ClaudeCode, OpenCode, Codex, and so on_.\"\n\nI tend to agree. But we also have to take into account that ClaudeCode and Codex both have an economic incentive to make you spend **more** tokens, not less. So from your list, I think OpenCode would be the most interested in implementing something like this natively if it really does improve things.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4710311819/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":2,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4711507900","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4711507900","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4711507900,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGNPnvA","user":{"login":"guplem","id":11029629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDI5NjI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11029629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem","html_url":"https://github.com/guplem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guplem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T19:17:14Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T19:17:14Z","body":"> both have an economic incentive to make you spend more tokens\n\nYeah, but... don’t they charge whatever percentage they feel like based on usage? I’m not familiar with Codex, but with Claude Code you don’t really know how many tokens you can use per session. They increase the percentage used, and it varies by model and even from week to week. So they could simply change the token–percentage relationship while reducing server load and costs. I don’t know how they would handle API users, though","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4711507900/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4712430647","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4712430647","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4712430647,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGOH8Nw","user":{"login":"Pyseph","id":45090858,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDkwODU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45090858?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph","html_url":"https://github.com/Pyseph","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T21:05:11Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T21:05:11Z","body":"Yeah, unfortunately I have zero incentive to even consider using this when there's a real risk in it degrading model performance. Actual benchmarks would be super appreciated.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4712430647/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4713114181","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4713114181","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4713114181,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGOxqRQ","user":{"login":"Pyseph","id":45090858,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDkwODU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45090858?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph","html_url":"https://github.com/Pyseph","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pyseph/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T22:52:29Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T22:52:29Z","body":"i ran a few benchmarks (for a total of 60 runs) across gpt-4.1-mini and gpt-5.4-mini and came back with this:\n\nmodel | without Ponytail | with Ponytail | median LOC\n-- | -- | -- | --\ngpt-4.1-mini | 15/15 passed | 10/15 passed | 11 -> 7\ngpt-5.4-mini | 15/15 passed | 14/15 passed | 15 -> 7\n\nso unfortunately it does seem to have a huge impact on model performance.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4713114181/reactions","total_count":13,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":9,"heart":0,"rocket":3,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4713179341","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4713179341","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4713179341,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGO1ozQ","user":{"login":"web-max","id":66029945,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MDI5OTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66029945?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max","html_url":"https://github.com/web-max","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-max/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T23:03:33Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T23:03:33Z","body":"> i ran a few benchmarks (for a total of 60 runs) across gpt-4.1-mini and gpt-5.4-mini and came back with this:\n> \n> model | without Ponytail | with Ponytail | median LOC\n> -- | -- | -- | --\n> gpt-4.1-mini | 15/15 passed | 10/15 passed | 11 -> 7\n> gpt-5.4-mini | 15/15 passed | 14/15 passed | 15 -> 7\n> \n> so unfortunately it does seem to have a huge impact on model performance.\n\nSad :(","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4713179341/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":3,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4715390449","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4715390449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4715390449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGQ8l8Q","user":{"login":"jeremyjpj0916","id":31913027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTEzMDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31913027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916","html_url":"https://github.com/jeremyjpj0916","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-16T05:48:49Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T05:48:49Z","body":"> i ran a few benchmarks (for a total of 60 runs) across gpt-4.1-mini and gpt-5.4-mini and came back with this:\n> \n> model\twithout Ponytail\twith Ponytail\tmedian LOC\n> gpt-4.1-mini\t15/15 passed\t10/15 passed\t11 -> 7\n> gpt-5.4-mini\t15/15 passed\t14/15 passed\t15 -> 7\n> so unfortunately it does seem to have a huge impact on model performance.\n\nNo free lunch <3","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4715390449/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4715673943","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4715673943","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4715673943,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGRN5Vw","user":{"login":"ryanmstokes","id":4103619,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDM2MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4103619?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanmstokes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanmstokes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-16T06:35:56Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T06:35:56Z","body":"> i ran a few benchmarks (for a total of 60 runs) across gpt-4.1-mini and gpt-5.4-mini and came back with this:\n> \n> model\twithout Ponytail\twith Ponytail\tmedian LOC\n> gpt-4.1-mini\t15/15 passed\t10/15 passed\t11 -> 7\n> gpt-5.4-mini\t15/15 passed\t14/15 passed\t15 -> 7\n> so unfortunately it does seem to have a huge impact on model performance.\n\nHaving this in your prompt \"The first lazy solution that works is the right one.\" is not a good idea even if it tries to counter that with \"when not to be lazy\" you should be trying to make the model not be lazy at all times and push back against it trying to implement the solution with least effort if it's not the correct one.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4715673943/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4715794761","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4715794761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4715794761,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGRVRSQ","user":{"login":"Maritolpixel","id":290220137,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUxoaQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/290220137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel","html_url":"https://github.com/Maritolpixel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maritolpixel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-16T06:54:48Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T06:54:48Z","body":"> i ran a few benchmarks (for a total of 60 runs) across gpt-4.1-mini and gpt-5.4-mini and came back with this:\n> \n> model\twithout Ponytail\twith Ponytail\tmedian LOC\n> gpt-4.1-mini\t15/15 passed\t10/15 passed\t11 -> 7\n> gpt-5.4-mini\t15/15 passed\t14/15 passed\t15 -> 7\n> so unfortunately it does seem to have a huge impact on model performance.\n\nI don't really understand what you're talking about, and I'm not going to use an LLM to pretend I do.\nBut I'd like to know, in a nutshell, what does the benchmark show?\nYou mention that it affects the model's performance, but... how do you know that? \n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4715794761/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4717440246","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4717440246","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4717440246,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGS5s9g","user":{"login":"DietrichGebert","id":137048761,"node_id":"U_kgDOCCsyuQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137048761?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DietrichGebert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-16T10:13:03Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T10:13:03Z","body":"Thanks for running this. The drop you saw was a bug in my benchmark, not the skill. The full writeup, code, and raw numbers are in #83, so you can re-run all of this yourself.\n\n**What was wrong:** my correctness check only counted code wrapped in fences, so bare code got marked wrong. The debounce task also tested for a different thing than it asked for. Both are fixed.\n\n**How I tested, and how many runs**\n\n1. Main benchmark. 5 everyday tasks (email validator, debounce, CSV sum, React countdown, FastAPI rate limit). Each task run 20 times per model, no-skill vs ponytail. I count lines of code and execute the generated code against test cases.\n\n| Model | Lines of code (no skill to ponytail) | Correctness |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| gpt-4.1-mini | 15 to 7 | 100% |\n| gpt-5.4-mini | 16 to 7 | 98% |\n| Claude (haiku, sonnet, opus) | about half | 100% |\n\n2. Edge-case stress test. 16 functions picked to trip lazy code, 20 runs each, no-skill vs ponytail: is_prime, factorial, fibonacci, gcd, binary_search, is_leap_year, days_in_month, int_to_roman, flatten, chunk, clamp, is_palindrome, plus email, url, credit card, ipv4. The traps are cases like is_prime(1), factorial(0), 1900 is not a leap year, target at the last index, deeply nested lists. Ponytail matched the no-skill baseline on every one. Each check proves itself first: it must pass a known correct answer and fail a known broken one before it scores any model output (run with `--selftest`, 16 of 16 pass).\n\n3. Email, the one real effect, tested harder (40 to 100 runs per model). Under ponytail, OpenAI models sometimes use a built-in called `parseaddr`, which extracts an address but does not check it, so it accepts junk like `@missing-local.com`.\n\n| Provider | Model | No skill | Ponytail | runs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OpenAI | gpt-4.1-mini | 100% | 98% | 100 |\n| OpenAI | gpt-4.1 | 100% | 79% | 50 |\n| OpenAI | gpt-5.4-mini | 100% | 92% | 100 |\n| OpenAI | gpt-5.4 | 100% | 98% | 50 |\n| OpenAI | gpt-5.5 | 98% | 94% | 50 |\n| Claude | haiku-4-5 | 88% | 100% | 40 |\n| Claude | opus-4-8 | 98% | 100% | 40 |\n| Claude | sonnet-4-6 | see note | 100% | 40 |\n\nNote on Sonnet with no skill: it returns a dict instead of a bool, so the strict test scores it 0. That is a return type quirk, not an inability. Read properly its logic is about 75%.\n\nI also tried 8 different skill-text edits to fix the OpenAI slip (60 runs each, plus one 100-run A/B). None helped and some made it worse, so I shipped no skill change. The reflex is in the OpenAI models, not the prompt.\n\n**Check it yourself** (in #83):\n\n```\ncd benchmarks\nnode robustness-audit.js --selftest    # verifies all 16 checks, no API key needed\nnode robustness-audit.js               # no-skill vs ponytail, gpt-5.4-mini, n=20\nAUDIT_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini node robustness-audit.js\n```\n\n**Bottom line:** ponytail roughly halves the code with no correctness cost on the edge-case suite, is 100% on email on Claude (its platform), and the only miss is email on OpenAI models, which is now documented.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4717440246/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4717828444","html_url":"https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65#issuecomment-4717828444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/65","id":4717828444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOS4HNr88AAAABGTRZXA","user":{"login":"dm13379","id":188513817,"node_id":"U_kgDOCzx-GQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/188513817?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379","html_url":"https://github.com/dm13379","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dm13379/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-16T10:41:53Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T10:42:46Z","body":"> > I’ve so far refused to use any because I always think, \"_If they were as good, they would be added to ClaudeCode, OpenCode, Codex, and so on_.\"\n> \n> I tend to agree. But we also have to take into account that ClaudeCode and Codex both have an economic incentive to make you spend **more** tokens, not less. So from your list, I think OpenCode would be the most interested in implementing something like this natively if it really does improve things.\n\nhttps://artificialanalysis.ai/agents/coding-agents?coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index&agents=claude-code-opus-4-7-medium%2Ccursor-cli-opus-4-7-medium%2Copencode-opus-4-7-medium#token-usage","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DietrichGebert/ponytail/issues/comments/4717828444/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"mini